      "rationale": "The archive has its native constructor and destructor. Bird, tower and rock bind their model and texture through the typed BML accessors, and rock stores its arrays as model and texture pointers. Allocation, release and texture binding retain the current source names at the same addresses. The historical rotation and scratch-vector access use the shared upstream layouts at the original addresses."
